From 39e263e91905fc436f6ed5ee94b84e14d9206acd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:29:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] test(verify): pin law (b)'s quarter arc reading on both
 sides; literal wall_arc_entry counts

- verify_arc_reading (new): a nominal arc round a convex wall passes
  where the old whole-tolerance chords convicted it (true clearance
  asserted); arcs past the floor round a convex wall and inside a concave
  one are convicted; an arc bowing 5 um past the floor into a straight
  wall, which the old chords hid, is convicted. With ARC_READ_SHARE set
  back to 1.0 exactly the two flip tests fail.
- wall_arc_entry: the bore takes exactly 5 arc entries; plunges are a
  literal 8; the seam check's comment says what it checks.
- arc_leads.rs: provenance names the public source of the lead shapes.
- decisions: the verdict flip and the STEP timing/budget bound.

Refs #689

