- verify_arc_reading: over radii 5-3000 mm (past the MAX_ARC_CHORDS clamp
  at r ~ 531 mm for the quarter reading, ~ 2125 mm for the old one) the
  quarter reading takes at least as many chords and its worst sagitta is
  never larger; below the clamp it stays within 2.5 um.
- decisions: an over-budget STEP mesh errs both ways (false gouge on a
  concave wall, a passed real gouge on a convex one); not introduced
  here (every mesh is at least as fine as before), removed for every
  model within budget, tracked for the rest in #864. The chord clamp's
  radius is named.

Refs #689

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
